1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
Three Dynamo Frontends are ready:

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,700
Pool A and Pool B at Hub, Remote Pool at Site.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,060
Hub ranks locally;

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,260
Site Gateway includes Remote Pool in a separate
snapshot.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,000
The Site Gateway sample is underway.

6
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:19,360
Each card separates its cumulative request counter
from requests attributed to

7
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,060
this sample.

8
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:21,640
This is an observed outcome,

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,420
not a weighted-share test.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,040
Pool B pressure begins.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,540
Pool B reaches four active requests.

12
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,640
Remote pressure begins next;

13
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:36,680
four is the comparison reference.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,100
As the Site Gateway sample advances,

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,080
requests are attributed to Pool A while Pool B and
Remote Pool remain at zero.

16
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,340
The Hub's published and consumed revisions match.

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,060
Remote Pool pressure is active;

18
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:05,620
recovery begins.

19
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,580
Remote Pool returns with a fresh zero-active
signal.

20
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,720
Scores and counters stay visible.

21
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,320
This remains the historical capture.

22
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,840
The final sample is still running.

23
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:27,200
Counts follow response attribution.

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,400
Eighteen valid responses;

25
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:32,740
all pools idle.
